#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/ternary.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.ternary.ternary:33
msgid ""
"Pass in either a file name to an ASCII data table, a Python list, a 2-D :"
"class:`numpy.ndarray`, a :class:`pandas.DataFrame`, an :class:`xarray."
"Dataset` made up of 1-D :class:`xarray.DataArray` data variables, or a :"
"class:`geopandas.GeoDataFrame` containing the tabular data."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/ternary.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.ternary.ternary:39
msgid ""
"Width of the ternary diagram. Use a negative width to indicate that positive "
"axes directions be clock-wise [Default lets the **a**, **b**, **c** axes be "
"positive in a counter-clockwise direction]."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/ternary.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.ternary.ternary:42
msgid ""
"[*amin*, *amax*, *bmin*, *bmax*, *cmin*, *cmax*]. Give the min and max "
"limits for each of the three axes **a**, **b**, and **c**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/ternary.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.ternary.ternary:47
msgid ""
"Set frame and axes attributes for the plot. It can be a bool, ``\"none\"``, "
"a :class:`pygmt.params.Frame` or :class:`pygmt.params.Axis` object. Raw GMT "
"strings or sequences of strings are also supported for backward "
"compatibility. If ``frame=True``, the frame will be drawn with the default "
"attributes. If ``frame=\"none\"``, no frame will be drawn. Use a :class:"
"`pygmt.params.Frame` or :class:`pygmt.params.Axis` object for more control "
"over the attributes of the frame and axes. A tutorial is available at :doc:"
"`frame and axes attributes </tutorials/basics/frames>`. Full documentation "
"is at :gmt-docs:`gmt.html#b-full`. For ternary diagrams, use :class:`pygmt."
"params.Frame` ``xaxis``, ``yaxis``, and ``zaxis`` attributes to set the "
"**a**, **b**, and **c** axes, respectively."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/ternary.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.ternary.ternary:58
msgid ""
"File name of a CPT file or a series of comma-separated colors (e.g., "
"*color1*,\\ *color2*,\\ *color3*) to build a linear continuous CPT from "
"those colors automatically."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/ternary.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.ternary.ternary:63
msgid ""
"Set the label for the *a* vertex where the component is 100%. The label is "
"placed at a distance of three times the :gmt-term:`MAP_LABEL_OFFSET` setting "
"from the corner."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/ternary.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.ternary.ternary:67
msgid "Same as ``alabel`` but for the *b* vertex."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/ternary.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.ternary.ternary:69
msgid "Same as ``alabel`` but for the *c* vertex."
msgstr ""

